      "name": "FindSlotByPattern",
      "signature": "void FindSlotByPattern(byte * szPattern)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Finds and initializes a slot matching the given pattern string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if system is initialized (g_dwInitialized)\n2. Acquire slot mutex lock\n3. Iterate through linked list starting at g_adSlotData comparing patterns\n4. When pattern matches, verify slot object (Ordinal_10013)\n5. If match found and count < 8, initialize slot (call Ordinal_10009/10010/10014/10011)\n6. Release mutex and return\n\nParameters:\n- szPattern (byte*): Pattern string to match against slot identifiers\n\nReturns:\n- void (always returns, status via side effects)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x58: Offset to slot ID field\n- 0x50: Offset to slot data pointer\n- 0x54: Offset to slot size\n- 0x5c: Offset to next slot pointer\n- 0x8: Maximum slots\n- 0xff: Clear/reset value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
