      "name": "CloseSoundStream",
      "signature": "void CloseSoundStream(int * pSoundHandle)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Closes and cleans up a sound/audio stream.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if handle is non-null and initialized (test pointer and first field)\n2. Acquire sound subsystem critical section lock for thread safety\n3. If stream slot is allocated (offset 0x12), close it via SAudCloseStream\n4. Call virtual destructor method via vtable at offset 0x0 (+0x48)\n5. Close underlying file handle via CloseFileHandle\n6. Clear stream slot (offset 0x12) and flags (offset 0x1c) to 0\n7. Release critical section lock and return\n8. If input is null/uninitialized, assert and fail via FUN_6f9e5965\n\nParameters:\n- pSoundHandle (int*): Pointer to sound stream structure containing vtable ptr, stream handle, state, and flags\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x12: Offset of stream handle field\n- 0x1c: Offset of flags field\n- 0x48: Offset in vtable for destructor method\n- 0x6f9f3c50: Address of sound critical section",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:6487b8031e820e8980be553303d571b9",
