      "name": "CloseSoundStream",
      "signature": "void CloseSoundStream(void * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Closes an audio stream and releases associated resources with thread synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input stream pointer is not NULL\n2. Check if stream has an active audio handle (offset 0x12)\n3. If handle exists, acquire sound critical section lock\n4. Close underlying audio stream via SAudCloseStream\n5. Invoke virtual destructor (offset 0x48 in vtable)\n6. Close associated file handle\n7. Clear stream reference and state flags\n8. Release critical section lock\n9. Call final cleanup on stream object\n\nParameters:\n- pStream (void*): Pointer to sound stream structure containing:\n  - [0x0]: Stream control flags/handle\n  - [0x12]: Audio stream handle (SAud*)\n  - [7]: Stream state flag\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function does not return a value\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x12 (18): Offset to audio stream handle within stream structure\n- 0x48 (72): Offset in vtable to destructor/cleanup function\n- 0x7: Stream state/flags field offset",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:a700127f92ddf2325aeeb14706e42949",
