      "name": "SetIntensity",
      "signature": "void SetIntensity(void * pObject, int nIntensity)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets object intensity/brightness value via virtual method call.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert pObject is non-null pointer, abort if validation fails\n2. Compare nIntensity parameter (0-255) against 0x80 (128) pivot\n3. If nIntensity > 0x80: Convert (0xff - nIntensity) to float, pass to Ordinal_10054\n4. If nIntensity < 0x80: Convert nIntensity to float, pass to Ordinal_10054\n5. If nIntensity == 0x80: Skip Ordinal_10054 call, use intensity 0\n6. Call virtual method at offset 0x40 in pObject's vtable with converted value\n7. Return void\n\nParameters:\n- pObject (void*): Pointer to object with virtual method table at offset 0x40\n- nIntensity (int): Intensity value in range 0-255 (0x80=128 is neutral)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value, may abort on null pointer)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x80 (128): Neutral intensity threshold dividing increase/decrease\n- 0xff (255): Maximum intensity, used for inverse calculation (0xff - value)\n- 0x40: Offset in virtual method table for intensity setter\n- 0x42fe0000: Float constant 127.0 used for normalization",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:c1028b66165e9789cd2a8dfecb27ebc3",
