      "name": "ConfigureFPUControlMask",
      "signature": "void ConfigureFPUControlMask(void * this, void * pCtx, dword dwLowerBound, dword dwMaskValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Configures FPU control word with masked bit pattern.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load mask parameter from stack\n2. Apply bitwise AND with 0xfff7ffff (clears bit 19)\n3. Push modified mask and original context pointer\n4. Call ModifyFPUControlWord with context, original value, and modified mask\n5. Pop cleanup registers\n\nParameters:\n- this (ECX): Object context from __thiscall convention\n- pCtx (stack): Context pointer passed to ModifyFPUControlWord\n- dwLowerBound (stack): Lower bound value (unused in this function, passed through)\n- dwMaskValue (stack): Mask value, bit 19 cleared before use\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xfff7ffff: Bitmask clearing bit 19 (disables exception precision control)",
