      "name": "ClassifyFloatValue",
      "signature": "int ClassifyFloatValue(int nLowBits, uint dwHighBits)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Classifies the type and sign of a floating-point number.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if double is NaN/Infinity (exponent all 1s)\n2. Check if subnormal or zero (exponent all 0s)\n3. Compare against zero threshold\n4. Return classification code based on sign bit\n\nParameters:\n- nLowBits (int): Low 32 bits of IEEE 754 double value\n- dwHighBits (uint): High 32 bits of IEEE 754 double value\n\nReturns:\n- Classification code: 0x200 (normal), 0x80 (negative), 0xc0 (positive), \n  or special: 4 (qnan), 2 (infinity), 1 (other special)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
