      "name": "ClassifyFloatSpecialValue",
      "signature": "uint ClassifyFloatSpecialValue(int nLow, uint dwHigh)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Classifies IEEE 754 floating-point special values based on exponent/mantissa patterns.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check for positive infinity (0x7ff00000) with zero mantissa \u2192 return 1\n2. Check for negative infinity (0xfff00000) with zero mantissa \u2192 return 2\n3. Check exponent bits (0x7ff8) for NaN markers \u2192 return 3\n4. Check for subnormal/denormal (0x7ff0 exponent, non-zero mantissa) \u2192 return 4\n5. Otherwise, not a special value \u2192 return 0\n\nParameters:\n- nLow (int): Low 32 bits of IEEE 754 double (mantissa lower)\n- dwHigh (uint): High 32 bits of IEEE 754 double (sign + exponent + mantissa upper)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Positive infinity\n- 2: Negative infinity  \n- 3: Not-a-Number (NaN)\n- 4: Subnormal/denormal floating-point\n- 0: Normal value or zero\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7ff00000: Positive infinity exponent (all exponent bits set, sign=0)\n- 0xfff00000: Negative infinity exponent (all exponent bits set, sign=1)\n- 0x7ff8: Exponent mask for NaN detection\n- 0x7ff0: Subnormal exponent pattern\n- 0x7ffff: Mantissa mask for zero check",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
