      "name": "ExtractFloatMantissaExponent",
      "signature": "float10 ExtractFloatMantissaExponent(float10 * __return_storage_ptr__, uint dwLo, uint dwHi, int * pnExponent)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "float10 *",
      "comment": "Extracts mantissa and exponent from a 64-bit IEEE double-precision float value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if input double equals _g_dblZeroThreshold constant\n2. For denormalized numbers (exponent bits are 0), shift mantissa left until normalized\n3. Count each shift as -1 exponent decrement from base -0x3fd\n4. For normalized numbers (exponent bits != 0), extract exponent field [20:31]\n5. Call FloatManipulateAndShift to normalize mantissa to [0.5, 1.0) range\n6. Subtract bias 0x3fe to get final exponent value\n7. Store exponent in output parameter, return normalized mantissa\n\nParameters:\n- dwLo (uint): Low 32 bits of IEEE 754 double (mantissa low)\n- dwHi (uint): High 32 bits of IEEE 754 double (sign/exponent/mantissa high)\n- pnExponent (int*): Output exponent value after normalization\n\nReturns:\n- float10: Normalized mantissa in [0.5, 1.0) range\n- Stores exponent value in *pnExponent parameter\n\nNotes:\nFor zero threshold: returns mantissa 0.0, exponent 0\nFor denormalized: initial exponent is -0x3fd (-1021)\nFor normalized: exponent is extracted from bits [20:31] minus 0x3fe bias",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:07c53c70ca23fa302c00136544982339",
