      "name": "FindFirstMatchingByte",
      "signature": "byte * FindFirstMatchingByte(byte * pbSearchStr, byte * pbCharSet)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "byte *",
      "comment": "Finds the first byte in pbSearchStr that matches any byte in pbCharSet.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 32-byte bitset to track which bytes appear in pbCharSet\n2. Scan pbCharSet (null-terminated) and set corresponding bitset bit for each byte\n3. Scan pbSearchStr and test each byte against bitset\n4. Return pointer to first matching byte, or NULL if none found\n\nParameters:\n- pbSearchStr (byte*): Null-terminated string to search\n- pbCharSet (byte*): Null-terminated set of bytes to match against\n\nReturns:\n- byte*: Pointer to first matching byte in pbSearchStr, or NULL if no match\n\nNotes:\n- Equivalent to strpbrk: finds first occurrence of any character from charset\n- Uses bitset for O(1) lookup instead of scanning charset for each byte\n- Handles all 256 possible byte values",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:0eb6c316488d30b6ee5d8d243ea3c5d6",
