      "name": "InitializeThreadLocalStorage",
      "signature": "dword InitializeThreadLocalStorage(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Initializes thread-local storage for manager subsystem.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize critical sections (synchronization objects)\n2. Allocate thread-local storage slot via TlsAlloc()\n3. Allocate manager context structure (0x74 bytes)\n4. Store context pointer in TLS slot via TlsSetValue()\n5. Initialize context: store current thread ID and 0xFFFFFFFF marker\n6. Return 1 on success, 0 on any failure\n\nParameters:\n- (none)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 (success): TLS initialized and context stored\n- 0 (failure): TlsAlloc failed, memory allocation failed, or TlsSetValue failed\n\nNotes:\n- Global g_dwTlsSlot stores the TLS slot ID for later retrieval\n- Context structure is 0x74 bytes allocated from heap\n- Each thread gets its own context pointer in TLS",
