      "name": "FormatFloatString",
      "signature": "char * FormatFloatString(char * szBuffer, size_t nMaxLen, int * pnSignAndExp, char chDecimalMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Formats a floating-point number string with proper sign and decimal placement.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve exponent value from pnSignAndExp[1]\n2. If decimal mode is set and exponent equals max length minus 1, adjust last digit to '0' and null-terminate\n3. Prepend minus sign to buffer if sign flag (pnSignAndExp[0]) is negative (0x2d)\n4. If exponent is less than 1, emit '0' digit before decimal separator\n5. Otherwise, advance position by exponent value\n6. If maximum length is positive, emit decimal separator character\n7. If exponent is negative, emit zeros to fill decimal places based on exponent magnitude\n\nParameters:\n- szBuffer (char*): Destination string buffer for formatted output\n- nMaxLen (size_t): Maximum length available in buffer for fractional digits\n- pnSignAndExp (int*): Array [0] contains sign flag (0x2d for negative), [1] contains exponent position\n- chDecimalMode (char): Mode flag; non-zero indicates decimal separator should be used\n\nReturns:\n- char*: Pointer to szBuffer (input parameter)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:1d26a9e5ce55b73c17db6b9f60fe2994",
