      "name": "FindHeapBlockByAddress",
      "signature": "dword * FindHeapBlockByAddress(dword nAddress)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "dword *",
      "comment": "Searches heap blocks to find entry containing specified address.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize search pointer to heap base (g_pHeapV3Current)\n2. Calculate heap end using base + (free_count * 0x14)\n3. Loop through heap entries (stride 0x14 bytes):\n   - Exit if reached end of allocated blocks (return 0)\n   - Check if nAddress falls within 0x100000 bytes of block base\n   - Return block pointer if match found\n   - Otherwise advance to next entry\n\nParameters:\n- nAddress (dword): Address value to search for in heap\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to heap block containing address range\n- 0 if address not found in any heap block\n\nNotes:\n- Heap blocks are 0x14 bytes in size\n- Each block has a base address at offset 0xc\n- Search range is 0x100000 bytes per block",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:2a0dd1f395da0f8e13609d337843c676",
