      "name": "ProbeStackSpace",
      "signature": "void ProbeStackSpace(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Probes stack space by touching pages before returning to caller.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load return address from caller context (ESP points to return address)\n2. Compare allocation size in EAX against page boundary (0x1000)\n3. If size exceeds page boundary, touch each page iteratively\n4. Touch pages by accessing memory at decreasing addresses\n5. After probing all pages, adjust ESP and return to caller\n6. On return, ECX has probe address, EAX has original size value\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: EAX contains allocation size in bytes\n- IMPLICIT: ESP points to caller's return address on entry\n\nReturns:\n- void (modifies ESP stack pointer, returns to caller)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1000 (4096): Windows page size in bytes\n- Stack probing is required before large local allocations to prevent stack overflow\n- Used by ValidateMsvcrtHeapSettings to prepare for large buffer allocation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:2a518bd4b0b93e6cf2e2d91eb6ff7bf6",
