      "name": "FindFirstCharNotInSet",
      "signature": "int FindFirstCharNotInSet(byte * pbSearchStr, byte * pbCharSet)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Finds first character in search string not present in character set.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Build bit-vector from character set using 32-byte array (256 bits)\n2. For each character in search string, set bit at (char >> 3)[char & 7]\n3. Scan search string, returning index of first char with unset bit\n\nParameters:\n- pbSearchStr (byte*): String to search\n- pbCharSet (byte*): Null-terminated set of characters to exclude\n\nReturns:\n- Index of first character not in set, -1 if string empty",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:30f0fd08cad97c1e8bd24ed371c4d8a2",
