      "name": "RemoveLinkedListNodes",
      "signature": "void RemoveLinkedListNodes(int * * ppHeadNode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Removes all nodes from a linked list whose value matches the first node, deallocating them via pool manager.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read head node pointer from ppHeadNode\n2. Extract first node's comparison value (pCurrentNode[0])\n3. Traverse linked list: for each node pIterNode, track previous node in pPrevNode\n4. Compare node value with first node: if match found, unlink and deallocate via ReleasePoolAllocation\n5. After removal, reload head pointer and repeat until no matching nodes remain\n6. Loop terminates when head becomes NULL\n\nParameters:\n- ppHeadNode (int **): Pointer to linked list head; updated when head node is removed\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x4: Byte offset to next pointer in node structure\n- 0xf0: Pool identifier for ReleasePoolAllocation\n- 0x6f9f0b28: Global context pointer for pool manager",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:314767313e8e907f63b2114e4ff97eb9",
