      "name": "FreeBufferResource",
      "signature": "void FreeBufferResource(void * pBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Frees a buffer resource with exception handling support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input buffer pointer (return if NULL)\n2. Check heap version (v2 or v3 support only)\n3. Set up SEH exception handler for cleanup\n4. Acquire mutex lock for thread-safe heap access\n5. Call appropriate heap free function based on version\n6. Release mutex lock and restore exception handler\n7. If buffer was freed successfully, return; otherwise call HeapFree directly\n\nParameters:\n- pBuffer (void *): Pointer to buffer to free\n\nReturns:\n- void (cleanup is implicit)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- g_nHeapVersion: Heap manager version (2 or 3)\n- 0x9: Mutex ID for thread synchronization",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
