      "name": "FreeLoopMemoryPages",
      "signature": "void FreeLoopMemoryPages(int nPageCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Deallocates the specified number of memory pages from loop structures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through linked list of loop nodes starting from PTR_PTR_LOOP_6f9f1374\n2. For each loop, scan its 0x400 page slots from highest address (0x3ff000) downward\n3. Deallocate pages marked as 0xf0 using VirtualFree with MEM_DECOMMIT (0x4000)\n4. Update freed count and decrement remaining page count\n5. Track lowest freed address for later garbage collection\n6. After deallocating pages, scan page map to detect empty loops\n7. If all 0x400 slots are marked as 0xffffffff, call RemoveLoopNode to deallocate loop structure\n8. Continue to next loop until target page count reached\n\nParameters:\n- nPageCount (int): Number of memory pages to deallocate (0x1000-byte chunks)\n\nReturns:\n- void",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
