      "name": "Log2F64",
      "signature": "double Log2F64(int nX, dword nY, int nZ, dword nW)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "double",
      "comment": "Compute logarithm base 2 of floating-point values using x87 FPU instructions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save FPU control word and check for valid precision\n2. Extract high/low dwords from parameters (pairs of int/uint form 64-bit doubles)\n3. Handle special cases: infinity, NaN, denormalized numbers\n4. Compute FYL2X (Y*log2(X)) where X and Y are FPU stack values\n5. Apply sign correction and FPU state restoration\n6. Return result on FPU ST0 register (as 80-bit extended precision)\n\nParameters:\n- nX: High bits of first 64-bit value\n- nY: Low bits of first 64-bit value\n- nZ: High bits of second 64-bit value\n- nW: Low bits of second 64-bit value\n\nReturns:\n- 80-bit floating-point result (stored in byte array)\n\nNote: FPU state management and special case handling required for IEEE 754 compliance.",
