      "name": "AreBitsUnset",
      "signature": "int AreBitsUnset(int * pBitArray, int nBitIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Checks if all bits from nBitIndex onwards are unset in bit array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if the bit at position nBitIndex is clear\n2. Starting from the next dword, verify all remaining dwords are 0\n3. Return 1 if all are clear, 0 if any bit is set\n\nParameters:\n- pBitArray (int*): Pointer to array of 3 dwords containing bit flags\n- nBitIndex (int): Starting bit position to check (0-95)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if all bits from nBitIndex onwards are unset, 0 otherwise",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
