      "name": "AcquireMutex",
      "signature": "void AcquireMutex(int nMutexId)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Acquires mutex by initializing critical section if needed, then entering it.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute critical section pointer from indexed table\n2. If entry is NULL, allocate CRITICAL_SECTION structure (0x18 bytes)\n3. If allocation fails, exit with error code 0x11\n4. Recursively acquire mutex 0x11 (protection during initialization)\n5. Double-check entry still NULL, then initialize critical section\n6. If not NULL, free the allocated structure (entry was initialized by another thread)\n7. Release mutex 0x11\n8. Enter critical section for caller\n\nParameters:\n- nMutexId: Index into critical section table (0-based)\n\nReturns:\n- void (always succeeds - calls __amsg_exit on malloc failure)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x18 (24): Size of Windows CRITICAL_SECTION structure\n- 0x11 (17): Special mutex ID used for protecting initialization",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5ba7875cbad7a3d5fce31ff25fd40455",
