      "name": "ProcessNumberDigits",
      "signature": "void ProcessNumberDigits(int * pResult, uint dwValue, int nSign)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes digits of a number value and writes them to output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Select positive/negative digit table based on nSign\n2. Divide nValue by 8 in loop, processing remainder with digit lookup\n3. For high-precision values, handle mantissa/exponent format\n4. Call ProcessNumberDigits for each digit group from table\n\nParameters:\n- pResult (int *): Output buffer for digit data\n- nValue (uint): Numeric value to process\n- nSign (int): Sign indicator (0 for positive, non-zero for negative)\n\nReturns:\n- void (writes to pResult buffer)\n\nRelated:\n- Calls FUN_6f9ecaca for digit conversion\n- Used by ParseNumberString, FormatFloatSignificand",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
