      "name": "InitializeCharClassTable",
      "signature": "void InitializeCharClassTable(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize character classification and mapping tables for the current code page.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetCPInfo to retrieve code page lead byte information\n2. Initialize character classification array (0x100 entries) with character values\n3. For each lead byte range, mark characters as 0x20 (locale-specific type)\n4. Fallback to ASCII-only mode if code page unavailable:\n   - Mark A-Z and a-z ranges with 0x10 (alphanumeric flag)\n5. Call helper functions to populate Unicode/locale-specific case mappings\n6. Iterate through character type table, updating classification and mapping globals\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: Uses g_dwCurrentCodePage global (current code page identifier)\n- IMPLICIT: Uses g_aCharType for character type information storage\n- IMPLICIT: Modifies g_abCharClassTable for character class flags\n\nReturns:\n- void (function modifies global tables in-place)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100 (256): Total character count for charset\n- 0x20: Locale-specific character class flag\n- 0x10: ASCII alphanumeric character flag\n- 0x80: Character property bit mask",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
