      "name": "ManagerStateInit",
      "signature": "void ManagerStateInit(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes manager state array by parsing string entries and allocating string copies.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if initialization is needed via g_fManagerInitialized\n2. Count non-'=' entries in g_pManagerState string buffer\n3. Allocate pointer array (count + 1 terminator)\n4. Iterate through manager state strings\n5. For each non-'=' entry, allocate and copy string via FUN_6f9e8470\n6. Set terminator, mark initialized\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: g_pManagerState contains manager configuration string buffer\n- IMPLICIT: g_fManagerInitialized tracks initialization state\n\nReturns:\n- void (initializes global state g_ppManagerStrings and g_fManagerReady)",
