      "name": "CopyStringAligned",
      "signature": "char * CopyStringAligned(char * szDest, char * szSrc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Copies a null-terminated string from source to destination with 4-byte-aligned bulk copying for performance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Align source pointer to 4-byte boundary, copying bytes one-by-one until aligned\n2. Copy 4-byte words while checking for null terminator using magic number check\n3. When null found, copy remaining 1-3 bytes and return\n\nParameters:\n- pszDest (char*): Destination buffer (caller must ensure sufficient size)\n- pszSrc (char*): Source null-terminated string\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to pszDest (destination buffer start)",
