      "name": "AdjustValueWithBitOps",
      "signature": "int AdjustValueWithBitOps(ushort * pwValueArray, uint * pdwResultBuffer, int * pnConfigParams)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Adjusts input values using bit-shifting and rotation operations based on configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract and process input value from word array\n2. Calculate delta based on difference from reference constant 0x3fff\n3. Check if all values are zero; if so initialize buffer\n4. Otherwise perform bit clearing, copying, and rotation operations\n5. Apply final bit mask based on configuration parameters\n6. Store results to output buffer\n\nParameters:\n- pwValueArray (ushort*): Input array containing value at offset 5 and related data\n- pdwResultBuffer (uint*): Output buffer to store final results\n- pnConfigParams (int*): Configuration array with parameters at offsets 0-5\n\nReturns:\n- 0 if all values are zero (early exit case)\n- 1 if specific conditions met during adjustment\n- 2 if normal adjustment path completed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7fff (32767): Mask for extracting value from word\n- 0x3fff (16383): Reference constant for delta calculation\n- 0x3ffe (16382): Adjustment threshold\n- 0x80000000: High bit flag for masking\n- 0x40, 0x20: Configuration selector values",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
