      "name": "CleanupSoundThreadEvent",
      "signature": "void CleanupSoundThreadEvent(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Closes and nullifies thread synchronization event handles.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify both event handles are valid (non-NULL)\n2. Signal the wait event to unblock any waiting threads\n3. Wait indefinitely for the thread event to complete\n4. Close both event handles\n5. Zero the handle pointers to prevent reuse\n\nParameters:\n- (none) - Accesses global event handles directly\n\nReturns:\n- void (always succeeds if handles are initialized)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeDirectSound: Creates the thread event handles",
