      "name": "CompareStringsInsensitive",
      "signature": "int CompareStringsInsensitive(void * this, void * pThis, byte * pbStr1, byte * pbStr2)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Case-insensitive string comparison with character table support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if character table is initialized (g_dwCharTableMode)\n2. If not initialized: use direct byte-by-byte comparison with fast normalization\n   - Add 0xBF to each byte, apply conditional 0x20 mask, add 0x41 to normalize case\n   - Continue until bytes differ or null terminator reached\n3. If initialized: acquire mutex, increment reference counter, acquire character table lock\n   - Use ConvertCharacterCase function for normalization via table lookup\n   - Compare normalized bytes until difference or null terminator\n   - Release locks and decrement reference counter\n4. Return comparison result (-1, 0, or 1)\n\nParameters:\n- pThis (void*): Context pointer used for character table operations\n- pbStr1 (byte*): First string to compare\n- pbStr2 (byte*): Second string to compare\n\nReturns:\n- 0 if strings are equal\n- -1 if pbStr1 < pbStr2\n- 1 if pbStr1 > pbStr2",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
