      "name": "ProcessDigitRounding",
      "signature": "void ProcessDigitRounding(char * szBuffer, int nDigitCount, int nContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Process floating-point digit string with rounding support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output buffer with first character '0'\n2. Copy up to nDigitCount digits from source, padding with '0' if source exhausted\n3. Null-terminate the string\n4. If rounding needed (source digit > '4'), increment last digit with carry propagation\n5. If first digit changed, update context counter; otherwise copy to destination\n\nParameters:\n- szBuffer (char*): Output digit string buffer (format: single digit + digits)\n- nDigitCount (int): Number of digits to copy\n- nContext (int): Context structure pointer at offset +0xc contains source, +0x4 contains counter\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xc: Offset in context for source digit pointer\n- 0x4: Offset in context for digit counter\n- '9'/'0': ASCII digit values for rounding carry\n- '4': Threshold for rounding (round if source > '4')",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
