      "name": "TerminateProcessCleanup",
      "signature": "void TerminateProcessCleanup(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Perform cleanup operations before abnormal process termination.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if initialization state is set or terminate flag is active\n2. If conditions met, write 0xfc to terminate handler\n3. If exit callback is registered, invoke it\n4. Write 0xff to terminate handler\n\nParameters:\n- (none)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- __amsg_exit: Calls this function during error handling\n- FUN_6f9e786c: Terminate handler that processes exit codes",
