      "name": "ConvertFloatingPointToString",
      "signature": "char * ConvertFloatingPointToString(double * pdValue, char * szResult, int nWidth, int nPrecision)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "char *",
      "comment": "Converts floating-point value to string representation with specified width and precision.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract mantissa and exponent from 64-bit floating-point value\n2. Store exponent information and digit array via FUN_6f9e835a\n3. Add sign character and format output using FUN_6f9e82e3\n4. Process remaining digits and null-terminate via FUN_6f9e63ba\n5. Return pointer to result buffer\n\nParameters:\n- pdValue (double *): Pointer to 64-bit floating-point value to convert\n- pszResult (char *): Output buffer for formatted string\n- nWidth (int): Field width for padding\n- nPrecision (int): Number of decimal places\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to pszResult buffer (same as input pszResult)",
