      "name": "InitializeExceptionRecord",
      "signature": "void InitializeExceptionRecord(uint * pExcRecord, uint * pStateFlags, uint dwConditionMask, uint dwRegisterValue, ulonglong * pData1, ulonglong * pData2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes Windows EXCEPTION_RECORD structure and related SEH context fields, then raises exception.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize exception record fields (indices 1, 2, 3) to zero\n2. Map input condition bitmask (dwConditionMask) to NTSTATUS codes via FUN_6f9ec7db\n3. Set field flags based on condition bits (bits 0x1, 0x2, 0x4, 0x8, 0x10)\n4. Invert param_2 flags and remap to output bit positions in field 2\n5. Query external state via FUN_6f9ec7db, set field 3 bits based on result\n6. Process field 0 bits 0-1 based on param_2 bits 0x400/0x800/0xc00\n7. Process field 0 bits 2-4 based on param_2 bits 0x300\n8. Encode dwRegisterValue into field 0 bits 5-15\n9. Set field 8 and field 20 (0x14) with specific bit patterns\n10. Copy 64-bit data from pData1 to field 4, pData2 to field 16 (0x10)\n11. Call FUN_6f9ec7e9 (cleanup hook), then RaiseException with NTSTATUS\n\nParameters:\n- pExcRecord (uint*): Pointer to exception record structure (at least 34 DWORDs)\n- pStateFlags (uint*): Pointer to state flags register (bits encode register choices)\n- dwConditionMask (uint): Input condition bitmask (bits 0x1-0x10 drive NTSTATUS selection)\n- dwRegisterValue (uint): 12-bit register value encoded at bit offset 5 in output\n- pData1 (ulonglong*): Pointer to 64-bit data copied to exception record[4]\n- pData2 (ulonglong*): Pointer to 64-bit data copied to exception record[16]\n\nReturns:\n- void (does not return - calls RaiseException which terminates execution path)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xc000008f, 0xc0000093, 0xc0000091, 0xc000008e, 0xc0000090: NTSTATUS exception codes\n- 0xfff: 12-bit mask for dwRegisterValue\n- Field indices: 1-3 flags, 4 data, 8 config, 16 (0x10) data, 20 (0x14) config",
