      "name": "InitializeCharacterTypeDetection",
      "signature": "BOOL InitializeCharacterTypeDetection(DWORD dwFlags, LPCSTR pszString, int cchSize, LPWORD pwCharClass, UINT dwCodePage, LCID lcid, int fUseUnicode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "BOOL",
      "comment": "Initializes and detects character type lookup capability (Unicode vs ANSI).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check cached detection method (DAT_6f9f3f24)\n2. If not cached, test Unicode support via GetStringTypeW(\"\")\n3. Fall back to ANSI support via GetStringTypeA(\"\") if Unicode unavailable\n4. Cache detection result and initialize character type lookup\n\nParameters:\n- dwFlags (DWORD): Character classification flags for GetStringType\n- pszString (LPCSTR): Input string to classify\n- cchSize (int): Character count in input string\n- pwCharClass (LPWORD): Output character class buffer\n- dwCodePage (UINT): Code page (0 = use default)\n- lcid (LCID): Locale ID (0 = use global default)\n- fUseUnicode (int): Force Unicode mode if non-zero\n\nReturns:\n- TRUE (non-zero) on success, FALSE (0) on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If code page is 0, uses g_dwDefaultCodePage\n- If LCID is 0, uses g_dwCharTableMode for ANSI mode\n- Unsafe stack allocation for wide character conversion (0x38 bytes)\n- ProbeStackSpace() called to ensure stack availability",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
