      "name": "ParseNumberString",
      "signature": "int ParseNumberString(void * this, void * pThis, ushort * pResult, int * pEndPos, byte * pInput, int nInputLen, int nRadix, int nFractionalDigits, int nAllowExponent)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Parses numeric string with optional exponent and sign, converts to signed integer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace (space, tab, newline, CR)\n2. Parse optional sign prefix (+ or -) with 0x8000 flag\n3. Parse optional leading zeros\n4. Parse mantissa digits (0-9) up to 0x19 (25) digits\n5. Parse optional decimal point (separator char)\n6. Parse optional exponent with sign\n7. Convert parsed digits to integer using digit accumulation\n8. Apply exponent shift, decimal/fractional adjustments\n9. Check overflow conditions and return status code\n\nParameters:\n- pThis: ECX context pointer (implicit)\n- pResult (ushort*): Output result array (mantissa low, mantissa high, flags)\n- pEndPos (int*): Output end position pointer\n- pInput (byte*): Input string buffer\n- nInputLen (int): Max input length/radix\n- nRadix (int): Digit accumulation mode\n- nFractionalDigits (int): Decimal adjustment\n- nAllowExponent (int): Allow E/e exponent parsing\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Valid parse\n- 1: Underflow error\n- 2: Overflow error\n- 4: No valid digits found",
