      "name": "CalculateSoundAttenuation",
      "signature": "float10 CalculateSoundAttenuation(float10 * __return_storage_ptr__, float flDistance, float flMaxDistance, float flReferenceDistance)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "float10 *",
      "comment": "Calculates logarithmic sound attenuation based on distance ratio.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If reference distance exceeds max distance plus tolerance, return minimum level\n2. If reference distance is below max distance minus tolerance, calculate attenuation:\n   - If reference equals zero threshold, use max distance as divisor\n   - Otherwise use reference as divisor\n   - Apply log2 formula: log10(2) * log2((max+min)/(divisor)) * attenuation scale\n3. Return maximum level for all other cases\n\nParameters:\n- flDistance (float): Current distance value\n- flMaxDistance (float): Maximum distance threshold\n- flReferenceDistance (float): Reference distance for comparison\n\nReturns:\n- float10: Attenuated sound level as extended precision float\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x4fe0: Function ordinal 10054\n- 0.3010299956639812: log10(2) constant for base conversion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
