      "name": "GetFpuStatusWord",
      "signature": "int GetFpuStatusWord(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Retrieves the FPU (x87 floating-point unit) status word and returns it as a signed integer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current EBP and allocate stack space\n2. Execute FNSTSW to store FPU status word to [EBP-2]\n3. Clear FPU exception flags with FNCLEX\n4. Sign-extend the status word (16-bit) to 32-bit integer in EAX\n5. Restore stack and return\n\nParameters:\n- None\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: FPU status word as signed int (bits 0-15 contain status, bits 16-31 sign-extended)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
