      "name": "GetThreadLocalStorageOffset",
      "signature": "DWORD * GetThreadLocalStorageOffset(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "DWORD *",
      "comment": "Returns a pointer to an offset location within thread-local storage.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize thread-local storage via InitializeThreadLocalStorage()\n2. Add 8-byte offset (2 DWORDs) to the returned base pointer\n3. Return adjusted pointer to caller\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: EDX typically contains context data passed through registers\n\nReturns:\n- DWORD*: Pointer to offset location within thread-local storage\n\nRelated Functions:\n- InitializeThreadLocalStorage: Allocates and initializes TLS structure",
