      "name": "HeapV3AllocateSlot",
      "signature": "dword * HeapV3AllocateSlot(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword *",
      "comment": "Allocates a new V3 heap slot with embedded buffers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if free count equals min size (heap needs expansion)\n2. If so, reallocate heap with 5x expansion plus 0x50 padding\n3. Calculate slot pointer from current heap base + free count offset (0x14 bytes per slot)\n4. Allocate 0x41c4 bytes from standard heap for field at offset 16 (pdwSlot[4])\n5. If successful, allocate 0x100000 bytes virtual memory for field at offset 12 (pdwSlot[3])\n6. Initialize slot: pdwSlot[2]=0xFFFFFFFF, pdwSlot[0]=0, pdwSlot[1]=0\n7. Increment free count and initialize first value at pdwSlot[4] to 0xFFFFFFFF\n8. Return pointer to slot or NULL on allocation failure\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwHeapV3FreeCount (current free slots)\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwHeapV3MinSize (minimum allocation size)\n- IMPLICIT: g_pHeapV3Current (heap base pointer)\n- IMPLICIT: g_hHeapManager (heap handle)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to new V3 heap slot structure (6 dword fields), or NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14 (20): Slot structure size in bytes\n- 0x50 (80): Heap expansion padding\n- 0x41c4 (16836): Buffer allocation size for slot[4]\n- 0x100000 (1MB): Virtual memory allocation for slot[3]\n- 0x2000 (8192): MEM_RESERVE flag for VirtualAlloc\n- 0x10 (16): Increment for min size growth",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b59a8a7d2c8fdcc2aac183f01f99a847",
