      "name": "CleanupCriticalSectionTable",
      "signature": "undefined CleanupCriticalSectionTable(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Cleans up and deallocates critical sections in the global critical section table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through each entry in the critical section table (g_pCriticalSectionTable)\n2. For each table entry, enumerate all critical sections within that entry\n3. If critical section is initialized (SpinCount != 0), call DeleteCriticalSection\n4. Clear the entry pointer to 0\n5. Continue until all table entries processed\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: Operates on global g_pCriticalSectionTable (array of critical section pointers)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x480 (1152): Size of critical section allocation block\n- 0x24 (36): Stride between critical section entries\n- 0xc (12): Offset to critical section structure within allocation",
