      "name": "MemMove",
      "signature": "void * MemMove(void * pDest, void * pSrc, dword nSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Optimized memory copy with overlap handling (memmove equivalent).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check for memory overlap (pSrc in [pDest, pDest+nSize])\n2. If overlap detected, copy backwards to avoid corruption\n3. If no overlap, copy forwards with dword optimization when aligned\n4. Align destination and source pointers as needed\n5. Copy bulk dwords (8+ at a time) and handle remainder bytes\n\nParameters:\n- pDest (void*): Destination buffer\n- pSrc (void*): Source buffer\n- nSize (dword): Number of bytes to copy\n\nReturns:\n- pDest: Pointer to destination buffer\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x4: Boundary for unrolled loop (8 dwords)\n- 0x3: Alignment mask (4-byte boundary)\n- 0x8: Unroll threshold (copy 8 dwords at a time)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
