      "name": "ParseNumericString",
      "signature": "int ParseNumericString(void * this, void * pContext, byte * pszString, int * pnEndPos, int nBase, dword dwFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Parses numeric string in specified base, handling sign and base auto-detection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace characters (lookup table check with flag 0x8)\n2. Handle optional sign: '-' sets FLAG_NEGATIVE (0x2), '+' ignored\n3. Auto-detect base if nBase==0: check for '0x' prefix (hex), '0' prefix (octal), else decimal\n4. Parse digits/letters checking against radix limit\n5. Check for overflow: compare accumulated value against max for base/flags\n6. Negate result if negative flag set\n\nParameters:\n- pContext (void*): Character lookup table context\n- pszString (byte*): Null-terminated input string\n- pnEndPos (int*): Output position where parsing stopped\n- nBase (int): Base 2-36 or 0 for auto-detect\n- dwFlags (dword): Control flags (0x1=signed, 0x2=negative, 0x4=unused, 0x8=parsed_ok, 0xc=overflow)\n\nReturns:\n- Parsed integer value, 0x7fffffff or 0x80000000 on overflow (depending on sign flag)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
