      "name": "LookupCharacterWithEncoding",
      "signature": "dword LookupCharacterWithEncoding(void * this, void * pContext, int nCharCode, dword dwMask)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Performs character code lookup with multi-byte UTF-8 encoding support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If character code in single-byte range [0, 0x100), use direct lookup\n2. For multi-byte characters, decode bytes and call conversion function\n3. Apply mask to result and return masked character value\n\nParameters:\n- pContext (void*): Implicit context (first operand in EDX for additional data)\n- nCharCode (int): Input character code to look up\n- dwMask (dword): Bit mask to apply to result before returning\n\nReturns:\n- Masked lookup result (ushort & dwMask)\n- 0 if multi-byte conversion fails\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100 (256): Upper bound for single-byte character range\n- 0x80: High bit mask for multi-byte character flag in lookup table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
