      "name": "ValidateAndGetAddressPool",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndGetAddressPool(uint dwAddr, void * * ppPool, uint * pdwPageBase)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates address alignment and retrieves corresponding memory pool.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search pool list starting from PTR_LOOP_6f9f1370 for pool containing address\n2. Verify address is 16-byte aligned (& 0xf == 0)\n3. Verify address lower 12 bits >= 0x100\n4. Return calculated size based on page-aligned base\n\nParameters:\n- pAddr (uint): Address to validate\n- ppPool (void **): Output pointer to containing pool node\n- pdwPageBase (uint *): Output page-aligned base address (pAddr & 0xfffff000)\n\nReturns:\n- Calculated size on success, 0 if validation fails or pool not found",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
