      "name": "GetEnvironmentStringsAnsi",
      "signature": "LPSTR GetEnvironmentStringsAnsi(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "LPSTR",
      "comment": "Gets environment variable strings in ANSI format, converting from Unicode if needed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check g_nEnvironmentMode to determine which API to use (GetEnvironmentStringsW or GetEnvironmentStringsA)\n2. If mode is 0, attempt GetEnvironmentStringsW; if successful, set mode to 1 (Unicode path)\n3. If mode is 1 or fallback, scan for environment block terminator (double null in wide chars)\n4. For Unicode path, convert wide char strings to ANSI using WideCharToMultiByte\n5. For ANSI path, scan for block terminator and allocate+copy buffer directly\n6. Handle allocation failures and conversion errors\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: g_nEnvironmentMode (global mode flag for caching API choice)\n\nReturns:\n- LPSTR: Pointer to ANSI environment strings buffer, or NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0: Initial uninitialized state for g_nEnvironmentMode\n- 1: Mode indicating Unicode API path (GetEnvironmentStringsW)\n- 2: Mode indicating ANSI API path (GetEnvironmentStringsA)\n- 0x1: Shift amount for wide char pointer arithmetic (divide by 2)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ee22dcb18299b51eb994a57f32a5df1d",
