      "name": "PrepareColorComponentsOnFPUStack",
      "signature": "void PrepareColorComponentsOnFPUStack(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Prepares color component values on FPU stack for integer conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 16 bytes on stack for two double values\n2. Exchange ST(0) and ST(1) on FPU stack\n3. Store ST(1) to stack as first component\n4. Store ST(0) to stack as second component\n5. Move high 32-bits from first component to EAX\n6. Call FUN_6f9e5b32 to convert and clamp values\n7. Deallocate stack space and return\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: ST(0) and ST(1) contain floating-point color component values\n- IMPLICIT: Values should be in range [0.0, 255.0]\n\nReturns:\n- void (results passed via FPU and subsequent stack operations)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
