      "name": "ProcessParameterType",
      "signature": "void ProcessParameterType(uint dwTypeCode, int * pTypeInfo, ushort * pwValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Processes parameter type codes from error handler, converting them to internal format IDs.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read type code from pTypeInfo, map to format ID based on type (1=8, 2=4, 3=0x11, 4=0x12, 5=8, 7=special, 8=0x10)\n2. Call FUN_6f9ec599 with format ID to validate/process type conversion\n3. If validation succeeds and type is 0x10/0x16/0x1d, set special type data and flags\n4. Call FUN_6f9ec2e6 with format ID and parameter data for conversion processing\n5. Call FUN_6f9ec7f8 for type cleanup\n6. Check error handler state with g_fErrorHandlerInitialized and call FUN_6f9ec7d8 if needed\n7. Call FUN_6f9ec7b0 with type code for final processing\n\nParameters:\n- dwTypeCode (uint): Type category code for parameter processing\n- pTypeInfo (int*): Pointer to type information array, pTypeInfo[0]=type code, pTypeInfo+2/4/6 contain type data\n- pwValue (ushort*): Pointer to value parameter\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10, 0x16, 0x1d: Special type codes requiring extended type data handling\n- 0x11, 0x12: Format IDs for specific type conversions\n- 0xffffffe3, 0xfffffffe: Bitmasks for flag field manipulation",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
