      "name": "SetSoundVolume",
      "signature": "void SetSoundVolume(int nVolume)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Sets the global sound volume level and applies it to all active samples.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if sound system is initialized via Ordinal_10002()\n2. Validate volume parameter is within 0-255 range\n3. Update global volume factor g_dwVolumeFactor\n4. Iterate through all active sound samples in linked list\n5. For each sample, calculate adjusted volume = (global volume \u00d7 sample base volume) / 255\n6. Account for muted state (set volume to 0 if g_dwSoundMute is set)\n7. Apply adjusted volume to actual sample buffer via virtual function at offset 0x3c\n\nParameters:\n- nVolume (int): Desired volume level (0-255), where 0 is silent and 255 is maximum\n- IMPLICIT: g_hSoundCriticalSection is locked for thread-safe access\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value; updates global state)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xff (255): Maximum volume value\n- 0x3c (60): Offset to SetVolume virtual function in sample object\n- 0x38: Offset to base volume field in sample structure\n- 0x34: Offset to flags field in sample structure\n- 0x4: Offset to next node pointer in linked list",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
