      "name": "WriteSoundBufferSlot",
      "signature": "dword WriteSoundBufferSlot(dword * pSlot, dword * pSample, dword dwSampleCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Write sound sample data to buffer slot with validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input parameters (slot, sample data pointer, count)\n2. Acquire critical section lock for thread safety\n3. Call Ordinal_10056 to convert sample data to audio buffer format\n4. Verify converted size doesn't exceed slot capacity\n5. Store converted buffer pointer and size in slot structure\n6. Call WriteSoundBufferData to write audio samples\n7. Mark slot as active (field +10)\n8. Update playback position field (+0c) if conditions met\n9. Release critical section lock\n\nParameters:\n- pSlot (dword*): Pointer to sound buffer slot structure\n- pSample (dword*): Pointer to sample data to write\n- dwSampleCount (dword): Number of samples to write\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success\n- Does not return on validation failure (calls FUN_6f9e5965)\n\nNotes:\n- Uses Ordinal_10056 for sample format conversion\n- Requires critical section synchronization (g_hSoundCriticalSection)\n- Performs assertion checks on capacity before writing",
