      "name": "InitializeSoundBuffer",
      "signature": "int InitializeSoundBuffer(int * pSoundInterface, dword dwSize, dword * pdwOutBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initialize a DirectSound buffer with zeroed memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert sound interface pointer is valid\n2. Enter critical section for thread safety\n3. Call interface method at offset +0x2c to allocate/prepare buffer\n4. Clear allocated buffer memory using optimized STOSD/STOSB loop\n5. Call interface method at offset +0x4c to finalize buffer initialization\n6. Exit critical section and return success (1) or failure (0 on error)\n\nParameters:\n- pSoundInterface (int*): Pointer to sound interface object (passed in ECX)\n- dwSize (dword): Size in bytes to allocate/initialize\n- pdwOutBuffer (dword*): Output pointer receiving initialized buffer address\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success\n- 0 on error (allocation failed or method returned negative value)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
