      "name": "InitializeAudioThread",
      "signature": "void InitializeAudioThread(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initialize audio playback thread and synchronization event.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if already initialized (g_hAudioThread != NULL)\n2. If initialized, trigger assertion failure via FUN_6f9e5965\n3. Create manual reset event for audio synchronization (CreateEventA)\n4. Create audio playback thread with LAB_6f9e2d80 as entry point (CreateThread)\n5. Store handles in global variables (g_hAudioEvent, g_hAudioThread)\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: Called from InitializeDirectSound after DirectSound setup\n\nReturns:\n- void (initializes global audio threading handles)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion fires if called multiple times (re-initialization protection)\n- Thread handle stored in g_hAudioThread for cleanup\n- Event handle stored in g_hAudioEvent for synchronization",
