      "name": "ValidateMsvcrtHeapSettings",
      "signature": "int ValidateMsvcrtHeapSettings(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates MSVCRT heap settings and checks Windows version compatibility.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call initialization routine FUN_6f9ea600()\n2. Retrieve Windows version info via GetVersionExA()\n3. Check if OS version is invalid (not v2) or pre-NT5 (pre-Windows 2000)\n4. If invalid, check __MSVCRT_HEAP_SELECT environment variable\n5. Normalize variable to uppercase and parse heap selection string\n6. If __GLOBAL_HEAP_SELECTED found, verify against module filename\n7. Extract heap specification from comma-delimited environment string\n8. Return appropriate status code (1-3) or call ExtractModuleVersionBytes()\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: Uses GetVersionExA() to obtain Windows version info\n- IMPLICIT: Reads __MSVCRT_HEAP_SELECT environment variable\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Success (valid Windows version detected)\n- 2: Heap selection error from FUN_6f9ea245()\n- 3: Default fallback or version extraction result\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x94 (148): Size of OSVERSIONINFOA structure\n- 0x16 (22): Length of \"__GLOBAL_HEAP_SELECTED\" string\n- 0x104 (260): MAX_PATH size for module filename\n- 0x1090 (4240): Size of environment variable buffer\n- 0x20 (32): ASCII offset for lowercase-to-uppercase conversion\n- 0x2c (44): Comma character (delimiter in env string)\n- 0x3b (59): Semicolon character (list separator)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:8315eedfd35b963ffd4ae4799f93ce60",
