      "name": "WriteSoundBufferData",
      "signature": "int WriteSoundBufferData(int * pSoundBuffer, uint dwStartOffset, int nCallbackParam, uint dwByteCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Writes audio data to the sound buffer using a callback to fetch source data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate sound buffer pointer and byte count\n2. Lock critical section for thread safety\n3. Call data callback to fetch initial data\n4. Loop: Copy data from callback output to circular buffer\n5. Adjust read position for circular wraparound\n6. Fill padding bytes with zeros if needed\n7. Unlock critical section\n\nParameters:\n- pSoundBuffer (int*): Sound buffer object with callback function pointers\n- nStartOffset (uint): Current read position in source\n- nCallbackParam (int): Parameter passed to data fetch callback\n- nByteCount (uint): Number of bytes to write\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success, 0 if callback fails\n\nNotes:\n- Uses circular buffer with wraparound logic at buffer end\n- Byte count adjusts for read position modulo (capacity-start offset)\n- Padding bytes (remainder after word copies) filled with 0",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:a1e8834f011a0c89a11eb63807d8b201",
