      "name": "FormatFloatSignificand",
      "signature": "dword FormatFloatSignificand(dword dwMantissaLo, dword dwMantissaHi, dword wExponent, int nPrecision, byte bRoundMode, short * pOutput)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Formats the significand (mantissa) of a floating-point number into decimal string representation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check for special values (exponent=0x7fff) and handle INF/NAN cases\n2. Extract exponent and mantissa components, apply bias adjustment\n3. Determine number of output digits based on precision parameter\n4. Perform long division to extract decimal digits via ShiftLeft/ShiftRight/Add operations\n5. Handle rounding: if last digit >= 5, increment previous digits and propagate carry\n6. Terminate string and return success indicator\n\nParameters:\n- dwMantissaLo (dword): Low 32 bits of 96-bit mantissa\n- dwMantissaHi (dword): High 32 bits of 96-bit mantissa\n- wExponent (dword): 15-bit exponent; bit 15 is sign (0=positive, 1=negative)\n- nPrecision (int): Desired output precision (number of fractional digits)\n- bRoundMode (byte): Rounding mode (bit 0: 0=truncate, 1=round to nearest)\n- pOutput (short*): Pointer to output buffer (formatted as short array for alignment)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success\n- 0 on special value (INF/NAN/SNAN/IND)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7fff: Exponent value indicating special value (INF/NAN)\n- 0x8000: Sign bit (1=negative exponent representation)\n- 0x3ffe: Minimum significant exponent for rounding adjustment\n- 0x134312f4, 0x4d, 0x4d10: Exponent bias calculation constants\n- 0x20/0x2d: ASCII for space/minus sign\n- 0xcc: Initialization padding pattern (0xFB=251, 0x3F=63)\n\nStructure Layout (output buffer):\n- [0]: Exponent (short)\n- [1]: Sign character (0x20=space, 0x2d=minus)\n- [2..N]: Decimal digits (ASCII '0'-'9')\n- [N+1]: Digit count (length)\n- [N+2]: Null terminator (0)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
